  "narrative": "The new stratified analyses strongly reinforce the central dataset-level findings while clarifying that STK11 loss does not show a meaningful negative association even when KEAP1-loss cases are excluded. H14, H15, H29, and H31 all support a large positive KEAP1-loss association in different contexts: excluding STK11 loss, within adenocarcinoma, excluding TP53 loss, and in higher-screen-quality cells. The signed estimates are approximately +0.78 to +0.82, far above the 0.15-unit threshold. I accept these as robust within-dataset associations, though they remain overlapping discovery analyses rather than independent replication. H16, H17, H30, and H32 similarly support a large negative raw SMARCA4-loss association: the signed positive estimates of about +0.78 to +0.83 for negative-direction claims correspond to raw decreases of similar magnitude. These persist after excluding KEAP1 loss, within adenocarcinoma, excluding TP53 loss, and in higher-quality screens, reducing concern that SMARCA4 loss is merely a proxy for KEAP1, TP53, subtype imbalance, or low screen quality. However, they are not independent samples, so SMARCA4 main-effect validation remains valuable. H18 is near zero: STK11 loss excluding KEAP1 loss has signed estimate +0.008 with interval from -0.068 to +0.085. This does not support the registered negative direction and is not meaningfully opposite beyond threshold. I reject H18 and close that exact STK11 refinement, while keeping interaction claims active only as secondary tests. For broader predictors, CDKN2A loss and PTEN loss are promising but not conclusively above the 0.15 threshold. H22 has point estimate +0.141 with interval +0.062 to +0.220; the point is below the threshold although the interval extends past it, so I keep it unresolved and active. H37 has point estimate +0.227 but lower bound +0.131, so the data are compatible with threshold-level negative raw association but do not demonstrate it at 95%; I keep it unresolved and request independent validation for H37 because it is the highest-value threshold uncertainty. H38 RB1 loss is close to null for a positive association: point +0.096, interval -0.002 to +0.195. The upper bound crosses threshold but the estimate and lower bound do not support a meaningful effect; I reject this registered claim and close it. I registered additional TP53-loss robustness comparisons because TP53-loss is accepted from one main discovery contrast but has not yet been shown to persist independently of KEAP1, SMARCA4, STK11, subtype, or screen-quality contexts. I also registered CDKN2A/MTAP and PTEN context refinements to separate co-deletion or co-mutation explanations. All conclusions are associations in this supplied dataset, not causal claims or evidence of external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted dataset associations: H7 KEAP1_loss positive, discovery+validated; H8 SMARCA4_loss negative, very strong discovery but not independently validated; H13 TP53_loss positive, discovery only. New accepted robustness claims: H14/H15/H29/H31 for KEAP1 in STK11=0, adenocarcinoma, TP53=0, high screen_roc_auc; H16/H17/H30/H32 for SMARCA4 in KEAP1=0, adenocarcinoma, TP53=0, high screen_roc_auc. These subgroup/stratum results are overlapping data, so they reduce confounding concerns but are not independent replication. H18 STK11 excluding KEAP1 is null and closed; overall STK11 registered negative remains rejected, but H19 interaction remains active only if co-loss modification is worth testing. Broad new claims: H22 CDKN2A loss point 0.141 with CI crossing threshold -> unresolved active; H37 PTEN loss point 0.227 with lower bound 0.131 -> unresolved active and selected for independent validation; H38 RB1 loss near null -> rejected closed. Next analysis priorities: newly registered TP53 robustness contrasts (TP53=positive excluding KEAP1/SMARCA4/STK11, adenocarcinoma, high screen_roc_auc), CDKN2A excluding TP53, MTAP excluding CDKN2A, PTEN excluding TP53, plus already registered interactions H19-H21 and technical context H33-H36 if needed. Do not accept marginal threshold-crossing intervals without independent evidence. Interpret all accepted claims as supplied-dataset associations only.",
